- 3-peer collaborative task management system (Alice, Bob, Carol)
- Creates documents independently, syncs via `CreateSyncState()` / `GenerateSyncMessage()` / `ReceiveSyncMessage()`
- Demonstrates all core Automerge features: maps, lists, text CRDTs, counters, nested structures
- Shows full document serialization (`Save()`), incremental updates (`SaveIncremental()`), and change history

**Sync Pattern:**
```csharp
using var syncAB = docA.CreateSyncState();
using var syncBA = docB.CreateSyncState();

for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    var msgA = docA.GenerateSyncMessage(syncAB);
    var msgB = docB.GenerateSyncMessage(syncBA);
    if (msgA == null && msgB == null) break;
    if (msgA != null) docB.ReceiveSyncMessage(syncBA, msgA);
    if (msgB != null) docA.ReceiveSyncMessage(syncAB, msgB);
}
```

**No Network/Storage:** Pure in-memory CRDT synchronization.

---

### **2. DEMOAPP.COLLABORATIVEDRAWING (Avalonia Desktop)**

**Purpose:** Collaborative drawing/diagramming tool (Figma-like)

**Structure:**
- **UI Framework:** Avalonia 11.3.11 with ReactiveUI
- **Main Window:** `MainWindow.axaml.cs`
- **ViewModel:** `CanvasViewModel` (manages shapes, layers, selection, tools)
- **Service:** `AutomergeService` (wraps `AutomergeDocument`)
- **Models:** `CanvasObject`, `Layer`, `ShapeType` (enum: Rectangle, Ellipse)

**Document Schema:**
```
root (map)
└── "layers" (list)
    └── [0..n] (map)
        ├── "name" (string)
        ├── "visible" (boolean)
        └── "shapes" (list)
            └── [0..m] (map)
                ├── "name", "type", "x", "y", "width", "height", "color", "zOrder"
```

**Document Lifecycle:**
1. User launches app → `DocumentSessionDialog` appears
2. Options: **Create** new, **Join** existing (by ID), **Resume** from local storage
3. **Create:** `RepoService.Repo.Create<object>()` → initializes layers/shapes structure → wraps in `AutomergeService.FromDocument()`
4. **Join:** `RepoService.Repo.Find<object>(documentId)` → loads from remote/storage → wraps in `AutomergeService.FromDocument()`
5. **Resume:** `RepoService.Repo.Find<object>(documentId)` → loads from local FileSystem storage

**ViewModels:**
- **CanvasViewModel:** Manages shapes/layers collections, handles UI commands (add/delete/move/resize shapes), listens to `DocHandle.Changed` events
- **ShapeViewModel:** UI representation of a shape (position, size, color)
- **LayerViewModel:** UI representation of a layer (visibility, shape list)

**Operations:**
- **AddShape:** Inserts shape object at default layer's shapes list
- **MoveShape/ResizeShape/RecolorShape:** Updates position/dimensions/color properties
- **RemoveShape:** List removal by layer index + shape index
- **AddLayer:** Inserts new layer with empty shapes list
- **RefreshFromDocument:** Rebuilds UI collections from CRDT state (called on remote changes)

**Network/Storage:**
- **RepoService:** Manages `Repo`, `FileSystemStorageAdapter`, `SignalRNetworkAdapter`
- **SignalR Connection:** To hub at `https://localhost:5001/hubs/documents` (or via Aspire service discovery)
- **Offline Mode:** If no RepoService, creates standalone `AutomergeService()`
- **Local Storage:** `~/.rayautomerge/CollaborativeDrawing/` (sharded by first 2 chars of document ID)

---

### **3. DEMOAPP.COLLABORATIVETEXTEDITOR (Avalonia Desktop)**

**Purpose:** Collaborative plain text editor with cursor synchronization

**Structure:**
- **Main Window:** `MainWindow.axaml.cs`
- **ViewModel:** `TextEditorViewModel`
- **Service:** `AutomergeService`

**Document Schema:**
```
root (map)
└── "content" (text)
```

**Key Features:**
- **Real-time Text Sync:** Two-way binding to `DocumentText` property
- **Cursor Preservation:** Uses `AutomergeCursor` to track cursor position across remote merges
  - Before edit: saves cursor via `GetCursor(position-1)`
  - After remote change: restores position via `GetCursorPosition(savedCursor)`
- **Diff-based Updates:** Compares old vs. new text, calculates prefix/suffix to minimize splice operations

**Operations:**
- **ApplyTextChange:** Simplified diff algorithm (find common prefix/suffix) → `SpliceText(index, deleteCount, text)`
- **RefreshFromDocument:** Updates UI text and cursor position on remote changes

**ViewModels:**
- **TextEditorViewModel:** Manages document text, cursor position, sync status, dispatches to UI thread

**Remote Change Handling:**
```csharp
void OnDocHandleChanged(object? sender, DocHandleChangeEventArgs<object> e) {
    if (e.IsLocal) return;
    _dispatcher(() => {
        SaveCursorBeforeEdit();
        RefreshFromDocument();
        RestoreCursorAfterEdit();
    });
}
```

---

### **4. DEMOAPP.COLLABORATIVEEDITOR (Avalonia Desktop)**

**Purpose:** Collaborative rich text editor with marks (bold, italic, underline, links)

**Structure:**
- **Main Window:** `EditorWindow.axaml.cs`
- **ViewModel:** `EditorViewModel`
- **Service:** `AutomergeService`
- **Model:** `FormattingState` (tracks bold/italic/underline at cursor position)

**Document Schema:**
```
root (map)
└── "content" (text with marks)
```

**Formatting System:**
- **Marks:** Applied to text ranges (start, end) with name (e.g., "bold", "italic", "underline", "link")
- **Mark Operations:**
  ```csharp
  MarkBold(start, end, value)      // Apply bold to range
  UnmarkBold(start, end)            // Remove bold
  GetMarks()                         // List all marks in text
  UpdateFormattingState()            // Determine bold/italic/underline at cursor
  ```

**ViewModels:**
- **EditorViewModel:** Manages text, cursor, selection, formatting states (IsBold, IsItalic, IsUnderline)
- Formatting buttons toggle marks on selected text
- Cursor movement updates formatting state via `UpdateFormattingState()`

**Block-level Structure:**
- Can split/join text blocks (paragraphs)
- Each block can have a type (e.g., "paragraph", "heading")
- Uses `GetSpans()` to segment text by marks and blocks

---

### **5. DEMOAPP.COLLABORATIVETASKBOARD (Avalonia Desktop)**

**Purpose:** Collaborative Kanban-style task board

**Structure:**
- **Main Window:** `MainWindow.axaml.cs`
- **ViewModel:** `BoardViewModel` + `ColumnViewModel` + `TaskItemViewModel`
- **Service:** `AutomergeService`
- **Models:** `Column`, `TaskItem`

**Document Schema:**
```
root (map)
└── "columns" (list)
    └── [0..n] (map)
        ├── "name" (string)
        ├── "order" (int64)
        └── "tasks" (list)
            └── [0..m] (map)
                ├── "title" (string)
                ├── "description" (string)
                ├── "status" (string)
                └── "votes" (counter — CRDT)
```

**Key Features:**
- **Horizontal Scrolling Board:** Columns as vertical cards with task list
- **Drag & Drop:** Move tasks between columns
- **Voting System:** Each task has a counter (`Increment(taskId, "votes")`) for upvoting

**Operations:**
- **AddColumn/RemoveColumn:** Insert/remove column from columns list
- **AddTask/RemoveTask/MoveTask:** CRUD on task items within column lists
- **UpvoteTask:** Increment counter (CRDT conflict-free merge)
- **UpdateTaskTitle/Status:** Modify task properties

**ViewModels:**
- **BoardViewModel:** Manages columns collection, handles remote changes via `DocHandle.Changed`
- **ColumnViewModel:** Holds column name, order, tasks list
- **TaskItemViewModel:** Task data (title, description, status, votes)

**Seeding:**
```csharp
void SeedDefaultColumns() {
    // Creates 3 default columns: "To Do", "In Progress", "Done"
    // Called after creating a new document
}
```

---

### **6. DEMOAPP.SHARED (Common Infrastructure)**

**RepoService:**
```csharp
public sealed class RepoService : IDisposable {
    // Manages Repo + FileSystemStorageAdapter + SignalRNetworkAdapter lifecycle

    public async Task InitializeAsync() {
        // 1. Create FileSystemStorageAdapter (local storage)
        _storage = new FileSystemStorageAdapter(storageDir);

        // 2. Create SignalRConnectionService (connect to hub)
        _connectionService = new SignalRConnectionService(...);

        // 3. Create SignalRNetworkAdapter (peer discovery + sync messages)
        _networkAdapter = new SignalRNetworkAdapter(_connectionService, ...);

        // 4. Create Repo (orchestrates storage + network)
        _repo = new Repo(new RepoConfig {
            Storage = _storage,
            NetworkAdapters = [_networkAdapter]
        });

        // 5. Connect and wait for ready
        _networkAdapter.Connect(_repo.PeerId);
        await _networkAdapter.WhenReady().WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10));
    }

    public Repo? Repo { get; }
    public PeerId? PeerId { get; }
    public ConnectionState ConnectionState { get; }
    public int PeerCount { get; }
    public event EventHandler<ConnectionState>? ConnectionStateChanged;
    public event EventHandler<int>? PeerCountChanged;
}
```

**RepoServiceOptions:**
- `HubUrl`: SignalR hub endpoint (e.g., `https://localhost:5001/hubs/documents`)
- `AppName`: Used in storage directory and for identification
- `StorageBaseDir`: Optional custom storage path (defaults to `~/.rayautomerge/{appName}/`)

**DocumentSessionDialog:**
- Shows 3 options: **Create**, **Join** (by ID), **Resume** (from local storage)
- Scans FileSystemStorageAdapter's sharded directory structure to find stored documents
- Emits `ResultReady` event with action + optional document ID

**ConnectionStatusBar:**
- Displays PeerId, connection state, server URL, peer count
- Updates in real-time as `RepoService` emits events

---

### **7. Program.cs Startup Pattern (All Avalonia Apps)**

```csharp
[STAThread]
public static void Main(string[] args) {
    IHost host = CreateHostBuilder(args).Build();
    App.Services = host.Services;  // DI available to views
    _ = host.StartAsync();

    BuildAvaloniaApp().StartWithClassicDesktopLifetime(args);
}

public static IHostBuilder CreateHostBuilder(string[] args) =>
    Host.CreateDefaultBuilder(args)
        .ConfigureLogging(...)
        .AddServiceDefaults()  // OpenTelemetry + health checks
        #if DEBUG
        .AddAvaloniaMcpConnector(...)  // MCP debugging
        #endif
        .ConfigureServices((context, services) => {
            string hubUrl = ResolveHubUrl();  // Aspire service discovery or fallback
            services.AddSingleton(new RepoServiceOptions { 
                HubUrl = hubUrl,
                AppName = "AppName" 
            });
            services.AddSingleton<RepoService>();
        });
```

**HubUrl Resolution:**
1. Aspire service discovery env vars: `services__api__https__0` or `services__api__http__0`
2. Fallback: `HUB_URL` env var
3. Default: `https://localhost:5001/hubs/documents`

**App.axaml.cs Setup:**
```csharp
public override void OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted() {
    if (ApplicationLifetime is IClassicDesktopStyleApplicationLifetime desktop) {
        var repoService = Services?.GetRequiredService<RepoService>();
        var vm = new CanvasViewModel(
            repoService,
            loggerFactory,
            action => Dispatcher.UIThread.Post(action));  // UI thread dispatcher
        desktop.MainWindow = new MainWindow { DataContext = vm };
    }
}
```

---

### **8. Document Creation/Loading Pattern**

**Create New:**
```csharp
async Task HandleCreateAsync(ViewModel vm) {
    if (vm.RepoService is null) {
        // Offline: standalone document
        var service = new AutomergeService();
        vm.SetAutomergeService(service);
        return;
    }

    await vm.RepoService.InitializeAsync();
    var handle = vm.RepoService.Repo!.Create<object>();
    await handle.WhenReadyAsync();

    // Initialize schema
    handle.Change(doc => {
        doc.PutObject(doc.RootId, "layers", AutomergeContainerType.List);
        // ... more initialization
    }, "Initialize schema");

    var document = ((IDocHandle)handle).GetDocument()!;
    var automerge = AutomergeService.FromDocument(document);
    vm.SetAutomergeService(automerge);
    vm.DocHandle = handle;  // Wire up remote change events
}
```

**Join Existing:**
```csharp
async Task HandleJoinAsync(ViewModel vm, string documentId) {
    await vm.RepoService.InitializeAsync();
    var handle = await vm.RepoService.Repo!.Find<object>(documentId, TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
    await handle.WhenReadyAsync();

    var document = ((IDocHandle)handle).GetDocument()!;
    var automerge = AutomergeService.FromDocument(document);
    vm.SetAutomergeService(automerge);
    vm.DocHandle = handle;
}
```

**Resume from Storage:**
```csharp
// Same as Join, but Find() loads from local storage first
// FileSystemStorageAdapter keeps documents in:
// ~/.rayautomerge/{appName}/{shard_prefix}/{remaining_id}/documents/*
```

---

### **9. Remote Change Synchronization**

**ViewModel listening pattern:**
```csharp
internal DocHandle<object>? DocHandle {
    set {
        if (_docHandle is not null) {
            _docHandle.Changed -= OnDocHandleChanged;
        }
        _docHandle = value;
        if (_docHandle is not null) {
            _docHandle.Changed += OnDocHandleChanged;
        }
    }
}

void OnDocHandleChanged(object? sender, DocHandleChangeEventArgs<object> e) {
    if (e.IsLocal) return;  // Ignore our own changes

    _dispatcher(() => {
        RefreshFromDocument();  // Rebuild UI from CRDT state
    });
}
```

**Why `IsLocal` check?** The same document object fires `Changed` for both local and remote updates. Local changes are batched/committed separately, so we skip them to avoid double-rendering.

---

### **10. AutomergeService Pattern**

Each app defines its own `AutomergeService` wrapping `AutomergeDocument`:

```csharp
sealed class AutomergeService : IDisposable {
    readonly AutomergeDocument _document;
    readonly bool _ownsDocument;  // Dispose document on cleanup?

    // Constructor: Create standalone
    public AutomergeService() {
        _document = AutomergeDocument.Create();
        // ... initialize schema
        _ownsDocument = true;
    }

    // Static Factory: Wrap existing document (from Repo)
    public static AutomergeService FromDocument(AutomergeDocument document) {
        var keys = document.GetKeys(document.RootId).ToList();
        if (!keys.Contains("expectedKey")) {
            // Initialize schema if missing
            document.PutObject(document.RootId, "expectedKey", ...);
        }
        return new AutomergeService(document, ownsDocument: false);
    }

    // CRUD methods (domain-specific)
    public void AddShape(...) { ... }
    public List<Layer> ReadCanvas() { ... }
    public byte[] Save() => _document.Save();
}
```

---

### **11. UI Structure (AXAML)**

All apps follow this pattern:

```xml
<Panel>
    <!-- Session Dialog (shown initially) -->
    <Border Name="SessionPanel" IsVisible="True">
        <DocumentSessionDialog />
    </Border>

    <!-- Editor/Canvas Panel (shown after document loads) -->
    <DockPanel Name="EditorPanel" IsVisible="False">
        <Border DockPanel.Dock="Top">
            <!-- Toolbar: tools, buttons, status -->
        </Border>
        <Border DockPanel.Dock="Bottom">
            <!-- Connection status bar + editor info -->
            <ConnectionStatusBar />
        </Border>
        <!-- Main content area -->
    </DockPanel>
</Panel>
```

**Visibility Toggle:**
```csharp
void ShowEditor(string? documentId) {
    sessionPanel.IsVisible = false;
    editorPanel.IsVisible = true;
}
```

---

### **12. Key Differences Between Apps**

| App | Data Model | UI Focus | CRDT Features Used |
|-----|-----------|----------|-------------------|
| **Drawing** | Layers + Shapes | Canvas drawing, layers panel | Maps, Lists, positioning |
| **Text Editor** | Single Text CRDT | Full-screen editor, cursor tracking | Text CRDT, cursors |
| **Rich Editor** | Text + Marks | Text + formatting toolbar | Text CRDT, marks, blocks |
| **Task Board** | Columns + Tasks | Kanban board, drag-drop | Lists, maps, counters (votes) |

---

### **13. Sync & Storage Summary**

**Network Sync:**
- **SignalR Hub:** `/hubs/documents` on API server
- **Peer Discovery:** Hub broadcasts peer presence, coordinates document subscriptions
- **Incremental Sync:** Automerge sync protocol (messages exchanged until converged)

**Local Storage:**
- **Adapter:** `FileSystemStorageAdapter`
- **Format:** Sharded directory structure (first 2 chars = shard)
- **Location:** `~/.rayautomerge/{AppName}/{shard}/{remaining_id}/`
- **Files:** Snapshots + incremental changes

**Offline Support:**
- If no RepoService or hub unreachable, apps create standalone documents
- Local-only CRDT sync (no peer collaboration)
- Can still save/load locally

---

### **14. ReactiveUI Integration**

All ViewModels inherit from `ViewModelBase` (Avalonia ReactiveUI):

```csharp
public class CanvasViewModel : ViewModelBase {
    ShapeViewModel? _selectedShape;

    public ShapeViewModel? SelectedShape {
        get => _selectedShape;
        set => this.RaiseAndSetIfChanged(ref _selectedShape, value);
    }
}
```

Commands are `ReactiveCommand<TInput, TOutput>`:
```csharp
AddRectangleCommand = ReactiveCommand.Create(() => SelectedTool = ShapeType.Rectangle);
SaveCommand = ReactiveCommand.Create(Save);
```

---

This structure provides a clean separation of concerns: **ViewModels** manage state & CRDT operations, **Services** wrap Automerge documents with domain logic, **RepoService** handles network/storage infrastructure, and **Views** bind to observable properties.

